#{[#edb/ref 17592186240337 1092 "Source question: 6.\n\nLet $0\\le a\\le b$ and let $f(x)\\ge g(x)$ on $[a,b]$.\n\nLet $R$ be the region on the $xz$-plane between $z=f(x)$ and $z=g(x)$ over $[a,b]$, and let $D$ be the solid region obtained by rotating $R$ around the $z$-axis."] [#edb/ref 17592186240342 1092 "Source question: 3."] [#edb/ref 17592186240382 1092 "Source question: 2.\n\nConsider the space curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle x(t),y(t),z(t)\\rangle\n=\\langle 3t,4t,5\\ln\\sec t\\rangle.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186240389 1092 "Source question: 4.\n\nOn the provided direction field sketch and label the following:\n\n![Direction field provided for Problem 4](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-1%2Fproblem-4-direction-field.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240419 1092 "Source question: 2.\n\nSolving initial value problems was an important application of integration from MTH 252. Recall that the function $y(x)$ satisfying\n\n$$\ny'(x)=f(x),\\qquad y(x_0)=a\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\ny(x)=a+\\int_{x_0}^x f(s)\\,ds.\n$$\n\nThe function $y(x)$ is known as the solution to the initial value problem. Solve the following initial value problems:"] [#edb/ref 17592186240432 1092 "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/4)\n\nIn this problem you will solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nxy'=9y-6x,\\qquad y(1)=-4.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186240433 1092 "Source question: 3.\n\nThe direction field for\n\n$$\ny'=\\frac{x}{y}\n$$\n\nis provided below. On the direction field sketch and label the following:\n\n![Direction field for y prime equals x over y](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-1%2Fproblem-3-direction-field.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240442 1092 "Source question: 1.\n\nThe electrical voltage in some 3D region is given by\n\n$$\nV(x,y,z)=x^3-5xy+xyz.\n$$\n\nConsider $P(2,8,5)$ and $\\mathbf v=\\langle 1,1,-1\\rangle$."] [#edb/ref 17592186240447 1092 "Source question: 3.\n\nThis problem will take you through the process of solving the initial value problem for the differential equation\n\n$$\ne^xy'+e^xy=0,\\qquad y(0)=y_0.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186240462 1092 "Source question: 1.\n\nThis problem will review the product and chain rule for derivatives, focusing on aspects that will be useful in this class."] [#edb/ref 17592186240472 1092 "Source question: 4.\n\nThe temperature in a room is given by the function\n\n$$\nw=f(x,y,z)=x^2+y^2+z^2.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186240599 1092 "Source question: 2.\n\n**Volume of a parallelepiped**\n\nConsider the slanted box formed by $\\mathbf u$, $\\mathbf v$, and $\\mathbf w$. Let $\\theta$ be the angle between $\\mathbf u\\times\\mathbf v$ and $\\mathbf w$.\n\n![Parallelepiped with base vectors u and v, side w, and normal u cross v](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-1%2Fparallelepiped-normal-and-height.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240645 1092 "Source question: 11.\n\nConsider $\\mathbf F(x,y)=-y\\mathbf i+x\\mathbf j$."] [#edb/ref 17592186240662 1092 "Source exercise: **1.1.3**, [printed page 7 (PDF page 19)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=19).\n\nYou have a system of $k$ equations in two variables, $k\\geq 2$. Explain the geometric significance of:"] [#edb/ref 17592186240723 1092 "Source question: 5.\n\nFor $x(t)=10-10\\cos t$ and $y(t)=3-3\\sin t$, with $0\\le t\\le2\\pi$, find all points with horizontal or vertical tangents. Give exact coordinate pairs as a comma-separated list; enter `DNE` if there are none."] [#edb/ref 17592186240768 1092 "Source question: 4.\n\n**The 2D gradient is orthogonal to a level curve**\n\nLet $\\varphi(x,y)$ be a scalar function and consider $\\varphi(x,y)=c$. From Problem 3, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=-\\dfrac{\\varphi_x}{\\varphi_y}$."] [#edb/ref 17592186240786 1092 "Source question: 4.\n\nConsider $x(t)=5\\sin t$ and $y(t)=5\\cos t$, where $0\\le t\\le2\\pi$. Use exact values."] [#edb/ref 17592186240787 1092 "Source question: 5.\n\n**Implicit differentiation — multivariable**\n\nLet $f(x,y,z)$ be a scalar function and consider the level surface $f(x,y,z)=c$. Regard $z$ as a function of independent variables $x$ and $y$, so $\\partial y/\\partial x=\\partial x/\\partial y=0$. The dependence tree is:\n\n![f depends on x, y, and z; each branch is differentiated with respect to x and y](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-1%2Fmultivariable-dependence-tree.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240802 1092 "Source question: 4.\n\nFor $x(t)=t^3-144t$ and $y(t)=2t^2$, find all points with horizontal or vertical tangent lines. Give exact coordinate pairs as a comma-separated list; enter `DNE` if there are none."] [#edb/ref 17592186240811 1092 "Source question: 1.\n\n**Area of a parallelogram**\n\nConsider the parallelogram formed by $\\mathbf u$ and $\\mathbf v$. Let $\\theta$ be the angle between them.\n\n![Parallelogram formed by u and v with included angle theta](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-1%2Fparallelogram-vectors.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240822 1092 "Source question: 9.\n\nConsider the spiral $x(t)=t\\cos t$, $y(t)=t\\sin t$, for $0\\le t\\le5\\pi$."] [#edb/ref 17592186240827 1092 "Source question: 6.\n\n**The 3D gradient is orthogonal to a level surface**\n\nLet $\\varphi(x,y,z)$ be a scalar function with level surface $\\varphi(x,y,z)=c$. From Problem 5, $\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}=-\\dfrac{\\varphi_x}{\\varphi_z}$ and $\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}=-\\dfrac{\\varphi_y}{\\varphi_z}$."] [#edb/ref 17592186240831 1092 "Source question: 6.\n\nConsider $x(t)=2\\sin t-3$ and $y(t)=2\\cos t+1$, with $0\\le t\\le\\pi$. Use exact values."] [#edb/ref 17592186240847 1092 "Source question: 3.\n\nFor $x(t)=t-6$ and $y(t)=5t+1$, with $0\\le t\\le2$, eliminate the parameter. Give exact answers."] [#edb/ref 17592186240931 1092 "Source question: 3.\n\n**Implicit differentiation — single variable**\n\nLet $f(x,y)$ be a scalar function with level curve $f(x,y)=c$. Regard $y$ as a function of $x$, so the dependence tree is:\n\n![f depends on x and y, and both branches depend on x](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-1%2Fsingle-variable-dependence-tree.png)"] [#edb/ref 17592186240957 1092 "Source question: 2.\n\nFor $x(t)=8t+1$ and $y(t)=t+8$, with $-\\infty<t<\\infty$, eliminate the parameter. Use exact values and fractions where needed."]}
